            <ArticleTitle>Chronic prostatitis/chronic pelvic pain syndrome.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>81-9; vi</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>In the 20th century, the term &quot;prostatitis&quot; traditionally referred to inflammation in the prostate, often attributed to infection. Prostatitis in this century usually refers to a chronic pain syndrome for which the presence of inflammation and involvement of the prostate are not always certain. This article discusses chronic prostatitis/chronic pelvic pain syndrome and the various factors associated with diagnosis and treatment.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
